<font face="helvetica,arial" size="4" color="00ff00"><b>The Plane of Hate</b></font>
</td>
<td>

<p align="justify"><font face="helvetica,arial" size="2" color="000000"><b>
Costs a very expensive stone to port there; very nasty level 50+ mobs run rampid; a chance for planar gear; the dreary, dark zone called the plane of Hate!
<br><br>
Six groups ported up to Hate, and successfully broke the port-in room, without one death, and proceeded to continue with battle plans.
<br><br>
The very first mob that we killed dropped some Iksar only Shaman gear, so I knew this would be an eventful night, right from the start.
<br><br>
The teamwork was outstanding, and the new aliance was like clockwork, as we took down one mob after another, making it look easy.
<br><br>
After about 20 pulls, the monks were starting to warm up, and SoD had already scored some unique planar loot.
<br><br>
Arthoes won the roll (being the only ranger there) on Thornyvine Vambraces, and a Revulent Whip (5/14). Bobmd also secured himself a pair of shiny, new Rune Etched Vambraces.
<br><br>
As soon as the surrounding mobs were killed, and Sector A was secure, we moved to Sector B (on the west wall camp) to continue our well planned assault.
<br><br>
Soon after our move, Memmree and Bipbop won some uber Cleric armor, (Memmree won a helmet, and Bipbop put on his new gaunts), while Jessandra got almost a whole suit of Bard armor.
<br><br>
Sector B clear! And it was time to consider pulling the Maestro, (one of the mini bosses in Hate). When everyone was buffed and ready to fight, 3 skilled pullers, Daylighte, Quchang, and Saedil worked together to pull him to the camp, where we proceeded to take him down.
<br><br>
It was not an easy fight, and many perished during the battle. Thiaz went LD but still fought like a champ, as she continued to beat him down until he lay motionless on the ground.
<br><br>
The Maestro dropped a Monk only mask, won by Saedil, (6ac, wt 0.1, effect: UV), who had died from the AoE blasts emitted by the Maestro, but was ressurrected in time to roll for the loot. <br><br>
From there, we moved to the Throne room and pulled some nasty hands, which turned out to be tougher than we could handle. After 3 attempts at the hands, we decided to call it a night.
<br><br>
Much fun was had by all attendees, and I thank you for your display of awesome teamwork. Its seems that our aliance with Mithril Blades will be a profitible one for all involved, and our first organized event together as an aliance went extremely well.
<br><br>
Congratulations to all who walked away with new armor and/or rare gems, and we look forward to hunting in the planes again.
<br><br>
For those of you who are not planes ready yet (level 46+), it's a fun place to hunt, and I encourage you to gain those levels needed to hunt with us in such exotic zones. Keep up the good work!
<br><br>
Bobmd Cureall<br>
Shaman of 56 Lunar Eclipses<br>
Guild Leader - SoD!
<br><br>

</b></font></p>
